From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: Format the word around the insertion point for SCF_WORD as msftedit does.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows 10 (x86_64 and i686, msftedit; winum
docs/wine-repro/riched20-scf-word-insertion-point, windows-2026-11-09 and
the boundary follow-up): EM_SETCHARFORMAT(SCF_SELECTION | SCF_WORD) at an
empty insertion point formats characters only when those on both sides of
the point are of the same class, and then the run of that class around
the point: the word (letters, digits, an apostrophe between them), the
punctuation, or between spaces the word before them together with the
spaces. At a word start or end, next to a different class, at the start
or end of the text nothing but the insertion point changes, whatever the
character formats. With a selection, SCF_WORD formats the selection only.

Wine formatted the next word with its trailing spaces, also at word
starts and ends. Inventor sets its normal font that way right after GD&T
symbol letters set in another face; the symbols turned into letters.

Limits: Windows' riched20 (RichEdit20W) differs from msftedit at word
ends before a space (it formats the word and the space); Wine registers
both classes with one window procedure and follows msftedit here. A point
right before a paragraph mark formats that mark on Windows; not done here
(todo_wine). Classes are decided with iswalnum; other scripts were not
measured.

v3 (2026-11-09): replaces v2, which was derived from the riched20 class;
the follow-up measurement showed the two classes differ, and msftedit's
rule is the simpler one that also covers Inventor's case. The test moves
to dlls/msftedit/tests/editor.c.
v2 (2026-11-09): replaced v1 (a word character on both sides), which
broke word ends before a space in riched20.

